WEBVTT

00:01.354 --> 00:02.950
&lt;i>Previously on:&lt;/i>

00:02.975 --> 00:04.425
Why don't you move in with me?

00:05.164 --> 00:06.103
What?

00:06.389 --> 00:08.106
Yeah, you and Ava
move in with me.

00:08.131 --> 00:10.565
I love you,
and I want you in my life,

00:10.590 --> 00:12.242
I want... I want
to have a future with you.

00:12.267 --> 00:14.845
If Ava and I move in,

00:14.870 --> 00:18.331
isn't somebody going
to have to move out?

00:20.854 --> 00:25.558
Hmm.

00:25.560 --> 00:28.644
Oh, yeah, yeah.
That's the ticket.

00:31.949 --> 00:34.683
Yes. Out with the bad.

00:36.453 --> 00:37.787
Morning.

00:37.789 --> 00:39.155
Morning.

00:39.157 --> 00:40.172
Hey, I'm glad you're up.

00:40.174 --> 00:41.357
I wanted...

00:41.359 --> 00:43.542
Oh, whoa.

00:43.544 --> 00:45.911
Sorry.

00:50.167 --> 00:52.034
Is that really
a good workout?

00:52.036 --> 00:54.420
Oh, yeah, yeah.
It's great for the circulation,

00:54.422 --> 00:56.872
stretches the spine.

00:56.874 --> 00:58.891
Your ball is hanging out.

00:58.893 --> 01:00.676
Oopsie-daisy.

01:00.678 --> 01:03.512
Back in the barn.

01:03.514 --> 01:06.215
Wha... All right, listen, uh,

01:06.217 --> 01:09.185
it's spring break this week,
so Zoey and her daughter

01:09.187 --> 01:11.387
are going to stay here.
Oh, that's nice.

01:11.389 --> 01:14.390
Yeah, it's kind of like
a... trial run.

01:14.392 --> 01:16.409
You know, see what it's like
to live together

01:16.411 --> 01:18.911
before we decide
to do anything permanent.

01:18.913 --> 01:20.329
Oh, that's a good idea.

01:20.331 --> 01:21.864
Living together is tricky.

01:23.067 --> 01:26.035
Ball.

01:26.037 --> 01:27.837
Sorry.

01:27.839 --> 01:29.088
Of course it's going
to be a little tight

01:29.090 --> 01:30.906
with all of us living here.

01:30.908 --> 01:32.574
Yeah.

01:32.576 --> 01:34.627
That's what I wanted
to talk to you about.

01:34.629 --> 01:37.430
Oh, don't worry. I'll tell Jake
to go to his mom's.

01:37.432 --> 01:38.914
Good, good.

01:38.916 --> 01:41.217
And I'll make myself scarce.
You won't even know I'm here.

01:43.137 --> 01:47.756
Oop.
Stepped on a duck.

01:47.758 --> 01:49.859
All right, actually,
I'm going to need you to, uh,

01:49.861 --> 01:52.945
move out for the week.

01:52.947 --> 01:54.596
What, wait, the whole week?

01:54.598 --> 01:56.399
Yeah, you and Zoey
don't really gel,

01:56.401 --> 01:58.284
so, I just thought
it'd be for the best.

01:58.286 --> 02:00.870
Oh, oh, that's fine.
Uh, but, uh, you know,

02:00.872 --> 02:04.039
just for the record, I gel
with pretty much everybody.

02:04.041 --> 02:07.910
I mean, ask around,
I'm positively gelatinous.

02:07.912 --> 02:10.579
I know, it's her.

02:11.915 --> 02:13.499
So, the plan is, I come
back after a week?

02:13.501 --> 02:16.635
Uh, you might want to think of
this as a trial run of your own.

02:16.637 --> 02:18.721
I mean, in case
Zoey and I do decide to

02:18.723 --> 02:20.122
live together permanently.

02:20.124 --> 02:22.308
Sure, sure, I get it.

02:22.310 --> 02:24.793
Uh, and, uh,
let me just add that

02:24.795 --> 02:26.562
no one is rooting for your
personal happiness

02:26.564 --> 02:28.013
more than I am.

02:28.015 --> 02:29.665
That's good to hear.

02:30.600 --> 02:32.852
Thanks, man.
Oh, no, no, no.

02:32.854 --> 02:36.155
Thank you, buddy.

02:40.243 --> 02:42.745
No reason to panic.

02:42.747 --> 02:45.481
Just got to find
a temporary new home...

02:56.560 --> 02:59.011
...and three new balls.

02:59.013 --> 03:01.330
♪ Men, men, men, men,
manly men, men, men ♪

03:01.332 --> 03:03.440
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

03:03.465 --> 03:06.865
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 9x21 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Mr. Hose Says Yes&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on April 16, 2012

03:06.866 --> 03:10.266
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

03:14.783 --> 03:17.452
What are you doing?
I'm taking a break.

03:18.954 --> 03:21.421
Didn't you just get here?

03:20.923 --> 03:22.739
Yeah.

03:24.442 --> 03:26.343
Anyway,

03:26.345 --> 03:29.396
I just wanted
to give you a heads up

03:29.398 --> 03:31.264
that Zoey's going to stay here
for the week.

03:31.266 --> 03:33.650
Uh-huh.
And she's bringing her daughter.

03:33.652 --> 03:35.519
How old?
Seven.

03:35.521 --> 03:37.020
See ya in a week.

03:36.522 --> 03:38.856
Oh, come on, Berta.

03:38.858 --> 03:41.141
You'll love her.
She's adorable.

03:41.143 --> 03:42.910
Maybe to her mother,

03:42.912 --> 03:45.446
and someone who's trying to get
into her mother's pants.

03:45.448 --> 03:48.499
All right, look, it's not going
to be any extra work for you.

03:48.501 --> 03:50.484
What ever Zoey doesn't
take care of, I'll handle.

03:50.486 --> 03:51.819
Really?

03:51.821 --> 03:53.871
You're going to take care
of a seven-year-old?

03:53.873 --> 03:55.673
Yeah.
We get a long great.

03:55.675 --> 03:57.675
And besides,
I got to learn sometime.

03:57.677 --> 04:01.795
I mean, if Zoey and I get
married, I'll be Ava's stepdad.

04:01.797 --> 04:05.966
You know, once upon a time,

04:05.968 --> 04:09.854
a cute little boy came to live
in this house for a few days.

04:09.856 --> 04:11.338
Maybe you've met him.

04:11.340 --> 04:14.475
He's the pot-soaked
masturbating couch potato

04:14.477 --> 04:17.344
who eats all your cookies.

04:17.346 --> 04:19.697
Is he the one who
finished off my macaroons?

04:19.699 --> 04:22.015
Your macaroons and my pot.

04:23.368 --> 04:27.655
My point being,
fool me once, shame on you.

04:27.657 --> 04:32.859
Fool me twice, I want a fully
funded 401 and a Camaro.

04:32.861 --> 04:36.080
Come on, Berta, it's just
going to be for a week,

04:36.082 --> 04:37.414
and it's just
the three of us.

04:37.416 --> 04:41.302
Really? Did Zippy
finally hang himself?

04:41.304 --> 04:43.170
No.

04:43.172 --> 04:44.705
He's going to
stay somewhere else.

04:44.707 --> 04:46.924
Zoey and I want to see what it's
like to live like a family,

04:46.926 --> 04:48.175
with a housekeeper.

04:48.177 --> 04:51.562
Who's got a retirement plan
and a muscle car.

04:51.564 --> 04:54.265
All right, look, Berta, if you
don't want to help me with this,

04:54.267 --> 04:55.816
I will find another housekeeper

04:55.818 --> 04:58.686
who's willing to do very little
work for a very large salary

04:58.688 --> 05:00.387
in a Malibu beach house.

05:00.389 --> 05:04.909
You're cute,
but you got a mean streak.

05:08.697 --> 05:11.749
All right, here we are.

05:11.751 --> 05:12.917
What do you think?

05:12.919 --> 05:14.702
Oh, boy, the ocean!

05:14.704 --> 05:16.654
Stay on the deck!

05:16.656 --> 05:20.174
Oh, she's so excited, she didn't
sleep at all last night.

05:20.176 --> 05:21.592
Yeah, I'm kind of excited, too.

05:21.594 --> 05:24.762
Really? I'm terrified.
Why?

05:24.764 --> 05:27.348
Well, because if this little
experiment doesn't work,

05:27.350 --> 05:29.249
it pretty much means
we're done, doesn't it?

05:29.251 --> 05:33.187
Wow, now I'm terrified, too.

05:33.189 --> 05:35.439
Oh, hey, there she is,

05:35.441 --> 05:37.391
the new queen of the castle,

05:37.393 --> 05:40.060
uh, milady.

05:40.062 --> 05:41.478
Hello, Alan.

05:41.480 --> 05:43.096
Thank you so much
for letting my boyfriend

05:43.098 --> 05:44.648
use his own house
for the week.

05:44.650 --> 05:46.033
Snidely put.

05:46.035 --> 05:47.985
Thank you.
So, where are you staying?

05:47.987 --> 05:51.205
Uh, well, I was thinking that
I was going to rent a suite

05:51.207 --> 05:53.290
at the Bel Air Hotel,
uh, but then I realized

05:53.292 --> 05:54.775
that cost money
and I have none.

05:54.777 --> 05:57.962
So, um, I'm just going
to stay with Lyndsey.

05:57.964 --> 06:00.798
How wonderful for her.

06:02.918 --> 06:04.718
So, um,

06:04.720 --> 06:07.120
all right, I will, uh,
I will see you in a week.

06:07.122 --> 06:08.672
See ya.
In a week.

06:08.674 --> 06:11.175
Yeah.
Say it.

06:11.177 --> 06:13.143
I'll see ya in a week.

06:13.145 --> 06:15.245
Okay, you two have fun.

06:15.247 --> 06:16.480
All right.

06:16.482 --> 06:18.682
Oh, oh, wait.
What room are you planning

06:18.684 --> 06:20.768
to put the little girl in?
Yours.

06:20.770 --> 06:23.270
Oh, oh, well, then I better

06:23.272 --> 06:24.605
get a few things out of there.

06:26.108 --> 06:27.574
Mostly magazines.

06:29.027 --> 06:30.477
Maybe we should put her
in Jake's room.

06:30.479 --> 06:32.646
No, that's actually worse.

06:33.782 --> 06:36.700
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:36.702 --> 06:38.318
You ready for another beer?

06:38.320 --> 06:40.037
Oh, aren't you a doll.

06:40.039 --> 06:42.623
You know...

06:42.625 --> 06:44.541
Eldridge is with his
father this week.

06:44.543 --> 06:46.660
Whoo, and Jake's with his mother.
Mmm.

06:46.662 --> 06:49.496
So, I guess we can
do anything we want.

06:49.498 --> 06:52.999
Yeah, and what do you want,
you dirty girl?

06:53.001 --> 06:56.220
Well, you know what would
make me really happy?

06:56.222 --> 06:58.171
Whatever it is,
I'll do it.

06:58.173 --> 07:01.859
The guest toilet is broken.
I want you to fix it.

07:04.229 --> 07:07.081
Uh, are we role-playing?

07:07.932 --> 07:10.234
Am I the naughty plumber

07:10.236 --> 07:13.954
here to snake your drain?

07:13.956 --> 07:16.457
No.

07:16.459 --> 07:20.677
You're the loving boyfriend
here to fix my toilet.

07:20.679 --> 07:22.346
Seriously?

07:22.348 --> 07:24.314
Seriously.

07:24.316 --> 07:26.717
Now?
Now.

07:26.719 --> 07:29.136
All right.

07:31.005 --> 07:32.506
Hey, uh, when you're
done with that,

07:32.508 --> 07:34.591
would you take the patio
furniture out of the garage

07:34.593 --> 07:36.060
and put it in the backyard?

07:36.062 --> 07:37.344
Sure.

07:37.346 --> 07:39.313
Make sure you wash it first.

07:39.315 --> 07:41.047
You got it.

07:41.049 --> 07:44.217
Yep, I got it, all right.

07:49.941 --> 07:52.392
I forgot a few things.
I'm going to run to the store.

07:52.394 --> 07:54.862
Oh, you know, relax.
I'll go for you.

07:54.864 --> 07:56.396
Actually, there's things
I need to buy

07:56.398 --> 07:58.565
that I'd rather
you not know I need.

07:58.567 --> 08:00.367
Say no more.

08:00.369 --> 08:02.836
Put your coat on, Ava.
I don't want to go-- I'm playing.

08:02.838 --> 08:04.905
Ava, come on.
No, she's fine.

08:04.907 --> 08:07.174
I'll watch her.
You sure?

08:07.176 --> 08:09.343
Yeah, of course.
It's no big deal.

08:09.345 --> 08:10.961
Do you want to
stay here with Walden?

08:10.963 --> 08:12.296
Yes, please.

08:12.298 --> 08:14.581
Okay. See you in about an hour

08:14.583 --> 08:16.817
Bye.
Bye.

08:19.522 --> 08:23.390
The sweet, sweet smell
of freedom.

08:28.263 --> 08:30.430
Oh.

08:30.432 --> 08:33.383
Hi.
I'm bored.

08:33.385 --> 08:35.536
I thought you were playing
with your dolls.

08:35.538 --> 08:37.621
I finished.

08:37.623 --> 08:39.823
What do you want to do?

08:39.825 --> 08:42.042
Well...

08:42.044 --> 08:44.928
(Cyndi Lauper's "Girls Just Want
to Have Fun" plays)

08:57.509 --> 09:00.110
♪ I come home
in the morning light ♪

09:00.112 --> 09:05.682
♪ My mother says, "When you
gonna live your life right?" ♪

09:05.684 --> 09:09.269
♪ Oh, mother dear,
we're not the fortunate ones ♪

09:09.271 --> 09:12.606
♪ And girls,
they want to have fun ♪

09:12.608 --> 09:17.528
♪ Oh, girls
just want to have fun ♪

09:22.467 --> 09:23.784
♪ ♪

09:23.786 --> 09:26.870
♪ The phone rings
in the middle of the night ♪

09:26.872 --> 09:31.258
♪ My father yells, "What you
gonna do with your life?" ♪

09:31.260 --> 09:35.112
♪ Oh, daddy dear, you know
you're still number one ♪

09:35.114 --> 09:38.882
♪ But girls,
they want to have fun ♪

09:38.884 --> 09:41.602
♪ Oh, girls just want to have ♪

09:41.604 --> 09:45.505
♪ That's all they really want ♪

09:45.507 --> 09:48.809
♪ Some fun ♪

09:48.811 --> 09:52.613
♪ When the working day is done ♪

09:52.615 --> 09:56.200
♪ Oh, girls,
they want to have fun ♪

09:56.202 --> 09:59.036
♪ Oh, girls just want
to have... ♪

09:59.038 --> 10:01.205
There's my good girl.

10:01.207 --> 10:02.522
Hi, Mommy.

10:02.524 --> 10:04.374
Where's Walden?

10:04.376 --> 10:06.326
Right there.

10:08.529 --> 10:11.048
He said it's his nap time.

10:12.233 --> 10:14.968
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:14.970 --> 10:18.371
I think I found your problem!

10:18.373 --> 10:20.424
You have got
a blown out fuse!

10:20.426 --> 10:21.508
Can you fix it?

10:21.510 --> 10:24.210
I don't see any
spare fuses but, uh,

10:24.212 --> 10:27.648
I do know a little trick.
What's that?

10:27.650 --> 10:29.066
Well, most people
don't know this,

10:29.068 --> 10:30.851
but you can use
an ordinary copper penny

10:30.853 --> 10:34.154
to replace a fuse.
No kidding?

10:34.156 --> 10:35.906
Yeah, electricians
won't tell you

10:35.908 --> 10:37.241
'cause they
want to charge you...

10:44.249 --> 10:47.067
It worked! The TV's back on!

10:47.069 --> 10:49.453
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:58.592 --> 11:00.742
"They were married
soon after,

11:00.744 --> 11:03.662
"and lived happily together
for many, many years.

11:03.664 --> 11:05.864
The end."

11:05.866 --> 11:09.067
Big surprise, huh?

11:12.855 --> 11:15.107
Thank God.

11:22.565 --> 11:24.733
It's too dark.

11:25.952 --> 11:27.953
Oh, sorry. Here you go.

11:27.955 --> 11:31.573
That's too bright.

11:32.441 --> 11:36.110
Okay. Uh... how about...

11:36.112 --> 11:40.332
I turn the bathroom light on
and leave the door open a crack?

11:41.334 --> 11:42.834
How's that?

11:42.836 --> 11:44.136
Better.

11:44.138 --> 11:45.137
All right.

11:45.139 --> 11:46.171
Good night.

11:46.173 --> 11:48.089
Did you look under the bed?

11:48.091 --> 11:52.060
No. Why, did you find
some funny magazines?

11:52.062 --> 11:55.147
You have to check for monsters.

11:55.149 --> 11:56.932
Oh.

11:59.769 --> 12:02.136
Nope, no monsters.

12:02.138 --> 12:04.138
Okay. Good night.

12:04.140 --> 12:05.657
What about the closet?

12:05.659 --> 12:07.192
What about it?

12:07.194 --> 12:09.327
Monsters.

12:10.863 --> 12:13.165
I don't want to have nightmares.

12:13.167 --> 12:15.200
Right.

12:15.202 --> 12:16.535
It's all clear.

12:19.755 --> 12:21.790
Aah... great.

12:21.792 --> 12:24.158
Now I'm gonna have nightmares.

12:24.160 --> 12:26.160
Okay, okay, good night.

12:26.162 --> 12:27.779
I'm thirsty.

12:29.164 --> 12:30.599
You're joking.

12:30.601 --> 12:32.968
Why would I joke about thirsty?

12:32.970 --> 12:34.519
Thirsty's not funny.

12:35.721 --> 12:37.772
I'll get you a glass of water.

12:37.774 --> 12:40.492
No, I want fizzy water.

12:41.343 --> 12:43.478
You want Perrier?

12:43.480 --> 12:46.347
Pellegrino would be fine.

12:46.349 --> 12:48.316
Okay.

12:48.318 --> 12:50.702
I'll go see what we have.

12:52.354 --> 12:54.122
How did the story end?

12:54.124 --> 12:56.491
Uh... they got married,

12:56.493 --> 12:59.728
and they lived happily together
for many, many years.

13:01.998 --> 13:04.132
Till they had kids.

13:05.585 --> 13:07.669
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:07.671 --> 13:09.087
How are you feeling?

13:09.089 --> 13:10.371
All right.

13:10.373 --> 13:13.258
My hand's still a little numb.

13:13.260 --> 13:16.377
Well, let's see if I can
make it all better.

13:16.379 --> 13:17.729
Mmm...
Ooh! Ooh!

13:17.731 --> 13:19.314
Make it all better.

13:19.316 --> 13:21.149
Daddy like.
Mmm...

13:22.986 --> 13:23.804
Did you hear something?

13:23.829 --> 13:25.797
Mm, nothing but the
rustling in my jammies.

13:27.324 --> 13:29.107
No!

13:29.109 --> 13:30.859
There's someone downstairs.

13:30.861 --> 13:32.661
No, there isn't. Come
on, make it all better.

13:32.663 --> 13:34.329
Alan!

13:34.331 --> 13:36.831
There's someone
in the house. Go look.

13:36.833 --> 13:40.735
Really? With a dead hand and
the beginnings of an erection?

13:40.737 --> 13:42.070
Go.

13:47.260 --> 13:49.461
And thus ends the erection.

14:14.071 --> 14:17.271
Who keeps their weed
in the crisper?

14:17.273 --> 14:19.941
What, you want to get
crispy, don't you?

14:25.164 --> 14:27.332
Ow!

14:34.473 --> 14:36.341
Good morning.

14:38.811 --> 14:40.929
It's still dark out.

14:40.931 --> 14:42.731
It's breakfast time.

14:42.733 --> 14:45.483
Maybe in London.

14:45.485 --> 14:46.851
What's going on?

14:46.853 --> 14:49.404
She wants breakfast.

14:49.406 --> 14:51.489
Okay.

14:51.491 --> 14:53.608
Just give me a minute.

14:53.610 --> 14:56.244
No, you sleep;
I'll get it.

14:56.246 --> 14:57.412
Thanks.

14:57.414 --> 14:59.698
That's it? No argument?

14:59.700 --> 15:03.001
Shh...

15:06.989 --> 15:08.707
All right.

15:08.709 --> 15:10.175
What do you want?

15:10.177 --> 15:12.961
Corn Flakes or Cheerios or...

15:12.963 --> 15:14.929
Eggs Benedict.

15:14.931 --> 15:17.098
Of course.

15:17.800 --> 15:20.268
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:19.770 --> 15:21.670
Watch your step.

15:21.672 --> 15:23.939
Yeah, wouldn't want
to get hurt.

15:27.843 --> 15:30.312
Those pain pills starting
to kick in yet?

15:30.314 --> 15:31.346
Oh, yeah.

15:31.348 --> 15:33.848
You could spread me on a toast.

15:35.034 --> 15:36.034
Okay.

15:36.036 --> 15:38.036
Let's get you into bed.

15:38.038 --> 15:40.205
No, no.

15:40.207 --> 15:41.856
Let's get &lt;i>you&lt;/i> into bed.

15:41.858 --> 15:42.857
Seriously?

15:42.859 --> 15:44.025
You want to fool around?

15:44.027 --> 15:45.494
Parts of me do.

15:45.496 --> 15:51.416
- Mr. Nose says, "No," but Mr.
- "Yes""

15:51.418 --> 15:53.218
Tell you what,

15:53.220 --> 15:56.871
why don't you just lie down
and let me take care of you.

15:56.873 --> 15:58.390
Really?

15:58.392 --> 16:00.976
You took care of me when I thought
there was someone in the house.

16:00.978 --> 16:02.377
Oh, right, right, I did.

16:02.379 --> 16:04.730
I was brave.

16:04.732 --> 16:07.232
Let's just get this belt
and zipper undone.

16:07.234 --> 16:09.884
Good thing you could breathe
through &lt;i>your&lt;/i> nose.

16:10.486 --> 16:12.721
- Ow! - What?!
Ball snag!

16:12.723 --> 16:14.356
Oh, sorry!
No, no, don't touch it!

16:14.358 --> 16:15.890
Don't...! Oh!

16:18.111 --> 16:21.480
I think I broke Mr. Hose.

16:32.508 --> 16:33.959
Hey!

16:33.961 --> 16:36.244
What?

16:36.246 --> 16:38.079
What in the hell
happened here?

16:38.081 --> 16:40.048
I tried to make breakfast
for the kid.

16:40.050 --> 16:41.883
"Tried"?

16:41.885 --> 16:44.553
Yeah. The eggs were too runny,

16:44.555 --> 16:48.307
so I made oatmeal
that was too dry,

16:48.309 --> 16:51.944
so I made waffles
that were-- and I quote--

16:51.946 --> 16:54.863
"Bloody dreadful."

16:54.865 --> 16:56.565
Where is she now?

16:56.567 --> 17:00.018
I don't know; I don't care.

17:00.020 --> 17:02.120
I can't do this, Berta.

17:02.122 --> 17:03.538
It's just... it's too much.

17:03.540 --> 17:05.240
She just never stops.

17:05.242 --> 17:07.542
Yeah, I raised
four daughters.

17:07.544 --> 17:11.330
The only thing that slows them
down is jail and johnsons.

17:12.248 --> 17:15.300
I told Zoey
we were gonna be a family.

17:15.302 --> 17:16.718
What am I gonna do?

17:16.720 --> 17:18.337
The kid's seven?

17:18.339 --> 17:19.388
Yeah.

17:19.390 --> 17:21.473
Wait nine years.

17:21.475 --> 17:22.891
What happens in nine years?

17:22.893 --> 17:26.595
If you're lucky, she runs away
with a coke-addled bass player.

17:26.597 --> 17:28.847
And if I'm not lucky?

17:28.849 --> 17:31.016
A drummer.

17:32.435 --> 17:34.736
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:38.157 --> 17:39.641
Hey.

17:39.643 --> 17:41.994
Oh, you're up.

17:41.996 --> 17:43.578
How are you feeling?

17:43.580 --> 17:44.780
A little better.

17:44.782 --> 17:45.947
I'm glad.

17:45.949 --> 17:48.417
Not looking forward
to ripping the Band-Aid

17:48.419 --> 17:49.835
off my scrotum, but...

17:49.837 --> 17:52.537
we'll cross that bridge
when we get to it.

17:52.539 --> 17:55.290
I'm so, so sorry.

17:55.292 --> 17:56.825
Yeah, just...

17:56.827 --> 18:00.495
FYI, if you'd like to try again,
I'm wearing sweatpants.

18:02.131 --> 18:04.016
No zipper.

18:04.018 --> 18:06.852
I cannot believe
you're still horny.

18:06.854 --> 18:10.188
Me neither,
but there it is.

18:10.190 --> 18:12.941
Well, I do owe you one.

18:13.977 --> 18:15.777
Oh, boy.

18:15.779 --> 18:17.029
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

18:20.950 --> 18:22.150
Do you smell that?

18:22.152 --> 18:23.151
Oh, don't worry.

18:23.153 --> 18:24.569
That's just the Neosporin.

18:24.571 --> 18:26.488
No.

18:26.490 --> 18:28.990
It-it smells
like something dead.

18:28.992 --> 18:31.710
It's not Mr. Hose.

18:31.712 --> 18:34.496
He's very much alive.

18:34.498 --> 18:36.998
Go ahead. Check.

18:37.000 --> 18:40.135
I think it's coming
from under the house.

18:40.137 --> 18:43.037
I'm sorry, I-I really
can't smell anything

18:43.039 --> 18:44.923
'cause of my broken nose...

18:44.925 --> 18:46.508
'cause of what you owe me.

18:46.510 --> 18:49.561
It-it's probably just a raccoon
or a possum.

18:49.563 --> 18:50.545
Hang on one sec.

18:50.547 --> 18:52.213
Let me call the exterminator.

18:52.215 --> 18:54.266
Oh, no, no, no,
that's going to take too long.

18:54.268 --> 18:57.853
I'll ju... I'll just get
a shovel and a garbage bag

18:57.855 --> 18:59.821
and deal with it.

18:59.823 --> 19:01.656
You're &lt;i>that&lt;/i> horny?

19:01.658 --> 19:04.659
I know, it's starting
to worry me, too.

19:07.915 --> 19:10.165
You okay down there?

19:10.167 --> 19:13.085
Yeah. Yeah, I think I see it.

19:15.089 --> 19:17.906
Looks like a-a dead possum.

19:17.908 --> 19:19.091
Be careful.

19:19.093 --> 19:21.093
Oh, don't worry about it.

19:21.095 --> 19:22.844
I-I'm just going
to shovel him into my...

19:22.846 --> 19:24.763
Not dead! Not dead!

19:24.765 --> 19:26.798
Ow! Ow!

19:26.800 --> 19:29.134
Yah! I'm sorry!
I'm sorry!

19:29.136 --> 19:30.769
I didn't mean...
Ow! No! Ow!

19:30.771 --> 19:32.437
Come on!

19:32.439 --> 19:35.089
Oh, that's going
to get infected.

19:35.091 --> 19:36.591
Ah! Ahh!

19:39.226 --> 19:40.510
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:44.291 --> 19:46.074
Thank you.

19:53.581 --> 19:54.882
Hey.

19:54.384 --> 19:56.750
Oh, hey.
Thanks for meeting me, man.

19:56.752 --> 19:58.752
Whoa!

19:58.254 --> 20:00.421
What happened to you?

19:59.923 --> 20:02.975
Well, let's see, uh...

20:02.977 --> 20:05.394
Electrocuted, got
my nose bashed in,

20:05.396 --> 20:08.280
and possibly rabies.

20:17.040 --> 20:19.107
How are you?

20:19.109 --> 20:22.127
I am really tired.

20:22.129 --> 20:24.413
My heart bleeds for you.

20:24.415 --> 20:28.133
Also my left ball sack.

20:28.135 --> 20:30.052
What's that smell?

20:30.054 --> 20:35.007
Oh, Neosporin, which
just a hint of possum.

20:36.559 --> 20:40.145
So, uh, how are things going
living with Zoey and her daughter?

20:40.147 --> 20:41.897
It's good, it's good.

20:41.899 --> 20:43.015
Oh.

20:43.017 --> 20:44.316
How's living with Lyndsey?

20:44.318 --> 20:45.734
Oh, it's terrific.

20:45.736 --> 20:47.903
That's great.

20:49.739 --> 20:51.907
That's great.

20:54.027 --> 20:56.912
If I could get rid of them...
Yes! A hundred times yes!

20:56.914 --> 21:00.914
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

00:01.500 --> 00:03.000
